    "reason": "HS-202-03, 2026-09-21: A1 falls 174 -> 106. The surface inventory of 2026-09-20 (SURFACE-INVENTORY-2026-09-20.md \u00a73.3) found the worst raw-HTML sites were the SHARED species themselves -- every menu item (DeskMenu), every wing tab (wings), the dock (7), the editor's rail (11) -- so a stranger's first five minutes met raw HTML at every turn. 68 sites on the five first-use jobs' screens now draw through the library Button, most of them through the new `chrome` variant (Signal.tsx): the species without the plate, for a verb whose material the strip it rides already draws. The residue (106) is the inventory's ledger -- WorkbenchWindow (23), the tool inspector (10), the Session/Coder/Thread pullouts, GroundingSection -- faces the five jobs do not touch. Only shrinks. The A1_RATCHET constant in tests/unit/test_ux_canon_ratchet.py carries the same number."
